  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Propanal and methanal undergo aldol condensation reaction with sodium hydroxide. The&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi></math>-unsaturated compound undergo&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></math>conjugated addition with cyanide ion gives a racemic&nbsp;mixture. The cyanide undergo acidic hydrolysis gives carboxylic acid.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/33d03f19-6a80-4647-93c7-50794c9da9ca-f0247494-7702-4af8-a6cd-674327490731-image.png\" style=\"width: 615px; height: 465px;\" /></p><p>Carboxylic acid will give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;gas, with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaHCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> solution</p>",
